From db7a1ba90b4c0e7a25b79b0610eed7fca0244f01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orgad Shaneh <orgad.shaneh@audiocodes.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:40:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] pcaputil: Decode through a jitter buffer paced by pcap
 time

Feed packets to a pjmedia jitter buffer in capture order and pull one
frame per ptime of pcap wall-clock time. This handles reordering,
duplicates, loss and jitter, and fills pauses with the real elapsed
time regardless of RTP timestamps, whether they understate the pause
(hold) or jump without one.

A pause longer than 30s is now filled unless the stream restarts
across it, which keeps a 30.5s hold in the same stream. Before a gap
longer than the buffer delay, buffered frames are played out, so a
short talkspurt is neither held back nor lost at end of file.

Add tests/pcaputil/pcaputil_test.py, which checks these cases on
synthetic streams.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
